     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nDear all,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nwe have now translated all the code in our 2012 book <i>&quot;Bayesian Population Analysis with WinBUGS&quot;</i> into JAGS, using either our preferred R interface package &#39;jagsUI&#39; or the older &#39;R2jags&#39;. You can download the entire book code for either interface on the\r\n<a href=\"https://www.vogelwarte.ch/en/research/population-biology/book-bpa/\" title=\"https://www.vogelwarte.ch/en/research/population-biology/book-bpa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.vogelwarte.ch/en/research/population-biology/book-bpa/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492663059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZYw8k8ffZNcEV7Q42Z2Rh\">\r\nbook webpage here</a> (scroll down and click on &quot;<a href=\"https://www.vogelwarte.ch/en/research/population-biology/book-bpa/#accordion=code-for-running-bpa-using-jags\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.vogelwarte.ch/en/research/population-biology/book-bpa/%23accordion%3Dcode-for-running-bpa-using-jags&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492663059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3yTCrMi1EmLKCgiqIKAWJe\">Code\r\n for running BPA using JAGS</a>&quot;).</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nFYI, we are currently working on a second edition of the BPA book, where we use NIMBLE as our main model-fitting engine, but will provide all book code also in the JAGS version on the website.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest regards  --- Marc &amp; Michael</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">_____________________________________________________________<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">Marc Kéry  ***** **<br>\r\n<a href=\"tel:+41%2041%20462%2097%2093\" value=\"+41414629793\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+41 41 462 97 93</a><br>\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">marc...@vogelwarte.ch</a><br>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.vogelwarte.ch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.vogelwarte.ch&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492663059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28GTri9JgLBoQXFpQbgkEl\">www.vogelwarte.ch</a><br>\r\nSwiss Ornithological Institute | Seerose 1 | CH-6204 Sempach | Switzerland<br>\r\n_____________________________________________________________<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">*** BOOKS: see <a href=\"http://www.hierarchicalmodels.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.hierarchicalmodels.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492663059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3f3TgkMqfqYmE3uwiPCctY\">www.hierarchicalmodels.com</a>  ***</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">- BRAND NEW:    Kéry &amp; Kellner (2024): ASM - Applied Statistical Modeling for Ecologists, Elsevier</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">- Schaub &amp; Kéry (2022): IPM - Integrated Population Models, Academic Press<br>\r\n- Kéry &amp; Royle (2021): AHM2 - Applied hierarchical modeling in ecology, Vol. 2, Dynamic and advanced models, Academic Press</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">- Kéry &amp; Royle (2016): AHM1 - Applied hierarchical modeling in ecology, Vol. 1, Prelude and Static Models, Academic Press\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">*** Hierarchical modeling workshops ***<br>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.phidot.org/forum/viewforum.php?f=8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.phidot.org/forum/viewforum.php?f%3D8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492663059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00L8h-dMWyEYdlzkZLAoa8\">www.phidot.org/forum/viewforum.php?f=8</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
